---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { LICENCE_URL } from '../config';

// Main libraries, from the app's workspace Cargo.toml; licences from their crates.
const libraries = [
  { name: 'egui and eframe', what: 'The interface and the window', licence: 'MIT or Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/emilk/egui' },
  { name: 'wgpu', what: 'Talking to the graphics card', licence: 'MIT or Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu' },
  { name: 'Vello', what: 'Drawing on the GPU', licence: 'Apache-2.0 or MIT', url: 'https://github.com/linebender/vello' },
  { name: 'kurbo and peniko', what: 'Curves, shapes and paint', licence: 'Apache-2.0 or MIT', url: 'https://github.com/linebender/kurbo' },
  { name: 'cosmic-text', what: 'Text layout and shaping', licence: 'MIT or Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/pop-os/cosmic-text' },
  { name: 'usvg (resvg)', what: 'Reading SVG files', licence: 'Apache-2.0 or MIT', url: 'https://github.com/linebender/resvg' },
  { name: 'image', what: 'Reading and writing pictures', licence: 'MIT or Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/image-rs/image' },
  { name: 'cpal', what: 'Playing sound', licence: 'Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/RustAudio/cpal' },
  { name: 'rfd', what: 'File dialogs', licence: 'MIT', url: 'https://github.com/PolyMeilex/rfd' },
  { name: 'AccessKit', what: 'Screen reader support', licence: 'MIT or Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit' },
  { name: 'ureq', what: 'Google Fonts and Figma requests', licence: 'MIT or Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/algesten/ureq' },
  { name: 'serde', what: 'Reading and writing project files', licence: 'MIT or Apache-2.0', url: 'https://github.com/serde-rs/serde' },
];
---

<Page
  title="Licence and credits"
  description="Emaki's licence (MIT or Apache-2.0), the FFmpeg it bundles, and the libraries, fonts and icons it is built on."
  heading="Licence and credits"
>
  <p slot="intro">Emaki is free and open source, and it stands on the work of many other open-source projects.</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Emaki</h2>
    <p>
      Emaki's code is licensed under either the <strong>MIT licence</strong> or the <strong>Apache License 2.0</strong>,
      at your option. {LICENCE_URL ? <a href={LICENCE_URL}>Read the licence</a> : 'The full text comes with the code.'}
    </p>

    <h2>FFmpeg</h2>
    <p>
      The Linux AppImage bundles <a href="https://ffmpeg.org">FFmpeg</a> (the <code>ffmpeg</code> and
      <code>ffprobe</code> programs) for reading video and audio and for export. FFmpeg is licensed under the
      <strong>GNU GPL version 3</strong>. Emaki itself is MIT/Apache-2.0 and only runs these programs; it isn't built
      from FFmpeg's code.
    </p>
    <p>
      FFmpeg's licence and a note on its source are inside the AppImage, in <code>usr/share/doc/emaki/</code>. The
      source is at <a href="https://ffmpeg.org/download.html">ffmpeg.org/download.html</a>, and the build recipe and
      exact sources of the bundled build are at
      <a href="https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds">github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Libraries</h2>
    <p>The main libraries Emaki is built with, each under its own licence:</p>
  </div>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="table stack">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Library</th><th scope="col">Used for</th><th scope="col">Licence</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          libraries.map((l) => (
            <tr>
              <td>
                <a href={l.url}>{l.name}</a>
              </td>
              <td data-label="Used for">{l.what}</td>
              <td data-label="Licence">{l.licence}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>Plus many smaller Rust crates, each with its licence listed in the code.</p>

    <h2>Fonts and icons</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/rsms/inter">Inter</a>, the app's interface font, by the Inter Project Authors, under
        the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://lucide.dev">Lucide</a> icons, in the interface and the Elements library, under the ISC
        licence.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> (MIT). It uses Inter and
      <a href="https://github.com/Outfitio/Outfit-Fonts">Outfit</a>, both under the SIL Open Font License, served from
      the site itself.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
